   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming a\ntransportation contract for the West Hempstead Union Free school district",
    "basePrintNo": "S5562",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5562-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5562\n\nSPONSOR: KAMINSKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming a\ntransportation contract for the West Hempstead Union Free school\ndistrict\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo provide a deadline waiver to the West Hempstead School District so\nthat they may receive reimbursement for a bus transportation contract\nfrom the State Education Department.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Paragraph a of subdivision 5 of section 3604 of the\neducation law.\n\nSection 2 directs the State Education Department to consider the specif-\nic contracts indicated in Section 1 of the bill.\n\nSection 3 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill allows the State Education Department to consider reimburse-\nment for a school bus transportation contract for the West Hempstead\nSchool District. Specifically, the contract addressed in the bill is\nE252155 from the 2017-2018 school year.\n\nThe contract is for legitimate student transportation costs incurred by\nthe district and is a reimbursable expense through the State Education\nDepartment. The aid cannot be reimbursed without special legislation due\nto technical errors in filing deadlines. Without the restoration of this\ntransportation aid, the school district would be faced with either\ncutting the quality and scope of its educational programs or raising\nreal property taxes. This would place an undue burden on district resi-\ndents and present hardships to many in the West Hempstead community.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
